{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse","id":1190042,"title":"The Trinity Multiverse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-02-27T16:06:40-08:00","id":1190042,"title":"The Trinity Multiverse","content":"Given that 'create universe' and cross-universe travel are a thing in Aberrant, and presumably also in Trinity (taint maddened though such universes may be), has anyone played any game of universe invasion, or multi-verse crisis?<br /> <br /> If a powerful enough Nova creates a universe, and that universe contains novas capable of creating universes, then some eventual multi-dimensional conflict seems inevitable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T20:34:27-08:00","id":1190117,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if anyone actually used Create Universe in a game vs &quot;this mechanic exists&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T20:55:14-08:00","id":1190121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1190117#post1190117\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not sure if anyone actually used Create Universe in a game vs &quot;this mechanic exists&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Right. Well... it's going to be a core premise of a game I'm starting next week, so I'll keep you posted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T21:15:16-08:00","id":1190126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CapitanTypo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1190121#post1190121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Right. Well... it's going to be a core premise of a game I'm starting next week, so I'll keep you posted.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On a player scale or as a background point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T21:34:42-08:00","id":1190134,"title":"","content":"I am planning some timeline travel between divergent histories<br /> <br /> Timeline Alpha: core timeline through Adventure!, Trinity Core, Aberrant, Anima, and Aeon<br /> <br /> Timeline Beta: core timeline until N-Day does not occur and Trinity Core action setting hones to the real world (includes comparatively harder scifi Expanse-style future with Talents, but no Novas or Promethean Chambers)<br /> <br /> Timeline Gamma: same as Alpha through Aberrant, but then the Aberrant War culminates in full burn - Mad Max/Fallout style setting ensues<br /> <br /> Timeline Delta: Inspiration Age (Adventure!) never ends and heroes and villains divert course of history leading to pulp space exploration by competing democratic, communist, and fascist powers by mid-20th Century, discovering a Burroughs-style Planetary Romance solar system<br /> <br /> Timeline Epsilon: Mal uses the Trinity test to set off the Nova Age in '45, Silver Age style setting by the 60s, Mal-Victorious Nova god kings ruling over human civilizations in their image in a 21st Century setting<br /> <br /> Timeline Zeta: War of the Worlds invasion in the 1890s, humanity rebuilding with the alien tech in the Edwardian Era create Promethean Chambers 200 years early<br /> <br /> Timeline Omega: Psions fail to rise against Colony's invasion; Aberrants destroy humanity","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-27T21:34:46-08:00","id":1190135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1190126#post1190126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> On a player scale or as a background point?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Background","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T08:43:44-08:00","id":1190288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1190134#post1190134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am planning some timeline travel between divergent histories<br /> <br /> Timeline Alpha: core timeline through Adventure!, Trinity Core, Aberrant, Anima, and Aeon<br /> <br /> Timeline Beta: core timeline until N-Day does not occur and Trinity Core action setting hones to the real world (includes comparatively harder scifi Expanse-style future with Talents, but no Novas or Promethean Chambers)<br /> <br /> Timeline Gamma: same as Alpha through Aberrant, but then the Aberrant War culminates in full burn - Mad Max/Fallout style setting ensues<br /> <br /> Timeline Delta: Inspiration Age (Adventure!) never ends and heroes and villains divert course of history leading to pulp space exploration by competing democratic, communist, and fascist powers by mid-20th Century, discovering a Burroughs-style Planetary Romance solar system<br /> <br /> Timeline Epsilon: Mal uses the Trinity test to set off the Nova Age in '45, Silver Age style setting by the 60s, Mal-Victorious Nova god kings ruling over human civilizations in their image in a 21st Century setting<br /> <br /> Timeline Zeta: War of the Worlds invasion in the 1890s, humanity rebuilding with the alien tech in the Edwardian Era create Promethean Chambers 200 years early<br /> <br /> Timeline Omega: Psions fail to rise against Colony's invasion; Aberrants destroy humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>Another timeline might involve a wiser Divis Mal who also finds a true love earlier in his life. He might procede in a more careful way and avoid some of his mistakes. Humanity moves out to the stars in the 21st century without the brutal violence. Then they meet the Doyne, who fear and loathe anyone with quantum powers. <br /> <br /> A war between humanity and agressive aliens.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T18:50:13-08:00","id":1190521,"title":"","content":"I'm running a game based on Baudrillard's concept of media representation creating reality. At the heart of the story is a taint ridden NPC whose power is a tweaked power boost that draws in social media trends and provides a boost to Quantum when used to enact something related to the trend from which the power is drawn. This peaks at the creation of universe that manifests the trend as a core principle of reality. <br /> <br /> It's going to be weird.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-02-28T20:48:03-08:00","id":1190548,"title":"","content":"I just had the idea of a post apocalyptic setting due to the Aberrant War war beimg even worse. The Aeon Foundation survived in its bunker fortress and was able to use its splitting edge engineers and scientists to 'build' Prometheus Chambers, create Psions, and form the Psi Orders. Of the later though foundations might be different they can be adapted to have the same themes and purposes. Part of the work is to fight aberrants and sub-aberrants, cleanse corruption zones, and rebuild civilization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T03:58:40-08:00","id":1190935,"title":"","content":"Parallel universes is one of the ideas I want to try when I first get to run a Trinity Game. I would love to scheme up some machinations involving puppetmasters pulling the strings of Two Earths, or introducing an Empire that instead of spanning the galaxy instead works to conquer parallel worlds. Or a secret society, maybe an alternate Aeon Society, that spans multiple Earths <br /> that agree to steer their worlds in wildly different paths so that the knowledge they reap is more diverse and less redundant when shared.<br /> Full of Ideas","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T09:40:49-08:00","id":1191015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1190935#post1190935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Parallel universes is one of the ideas I want to try when I first get to run a Trinity Game. I would love to scheme up some machinations involving puppetmasters pulling the strings of Two Earths, or introducing an Empire that instead of spanning the galaxy instead works to conquer parallel worlds. Or a secret society, maybe an alternate Aeon Society, that spans multiple Earths<br /> that agree to steer their worlds in wildly different paths so that the knowledge they reap is more diverse and less redundant when shared.<br /> Full of Ideas</div> </div> </div> </div>I love a multiverse-spanning Aeon. I wonder if there's an &quot;Earth Prime&quot; in this and they're directing the alternate worlds. Like there's exactly only one Maxwell Mercer and he flits between them all. I kinda dig a version of this that one of the Aeons went amuck (maybe Michael Donighal takes the reins) and is creating a pan-reality empire with their learned dictatorship and master of arcane energies (flux, quantum, psi) at the top.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T18:53:04-08:00","id":1191194,"title":"","content":"I just thought about something. So in the Chinese Ultimatum the Novas were allowed to depart for Luna, though they left the sole system entirely. <br /> <br /> Well imagine if they choose that option. If Divis Mal and the others went there rather then fully depart. You have baseline Earth within earshot of nova moon. <br /> <br /> I figure Divis Mal cleans house, removing the super corrupted and sets up a nova government, then gets board and leaves. That way his presence is there as backstory but not to overshadow the eventual PCs. <br /> <br /> It would be intriguing because I'm not sure the Doyen could do there shenanigans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T22:35:37-08:00","id":1191255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191194#post1191194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just thought about something. So in the Chinese Ultimatum the Novas were allowed to depart for Luna, though they left the sole system entirely. <br /> <br /> Well imagine if they choose that option. If Divis Mal and the others went there rather then fully depart. You have baseline Earth within earshot of nova moon. <br /> <br /> I figure Divis Mal cleans house, removing the super corrupted and sets up a nova government, then gets board and leaves. That way his presence is there as backstory but not to overshadow the eventual PCs. <br /> <br /> It would be intriguing because I'm not sure the Doyen could do there shenanigans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m pretty sure they would Nuke the moon if they accepted, though some Novas would survive. It seems pretty likely the moon wouldn\u2019t have been safe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-02T22:56:26-08:00","id":1191259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191255#post1191255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019m pretty sure they would Nuke the moon if they accepted, though some Novas would survive. It seems pretty likely the moon wouldn\u2019t have been safe.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Chinese Ultimatum actually is &quot;leave Earth, but you can go to the moon if you want.&quot; So technically it was allowed. <br /> <br /> And since I'm a believer in more hopeful sagas I consider things would work out well eventually. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T01:36:54-08:00","id":1191286,"title":"","content":"Oh I know the offer was space on the moon, but I believe the Novas understood it would not be safe, if they were willing to blow up their own home world to be rid of the Novas, then having all the beings they hate and fear in one small moon would be understood as too tempting a target. Are you really going to trust such people not to blow you up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-03T05:40:50-08:00","id":1191318,"title":"","content":"Another possibility is to change the world long ago. Picture an alchemist, maybe Famel or Bacon, accidentally taps into telluric energies. Start the Inspiration Age in the late middle ages or the very start of the early modern period.<br /> <br /> Picture Elizabeth I as a Stalwart. John Dee could be a Mesmerist. Oh how could you list the Daredevils?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:33:38-08:00","id":1191635,"title":"","content":"The Continuum allows for alternate timelines. A Multiverse would allow for alternate <i>realities</i>, with differences too drastic even for the Butterfly Effect to account for. For instance, a universe where the other planets in the Solar System are habitable, or where there's a vast galactic community of aliens (instead of aliens being rare and either ding off or transcending after \u201conly\u201d 10,000 years). Or where Earth is populated by anthropomorphic animals instead of humans. Or where the gods of myth are <i>real</i>, and coexist with humanity as it expands to the stars.<br /> <br /> Considering that each such alternate universe would have its own Continuum of alternate histories, you probably wouldn't need many universes in the Trinity Multiverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:47:00-08:00","id":1191640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191318#post1191318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another possibility is to change the world long ago. Picture an alchemist, maybe Famel or Bacon, accidentally taps into telluric energies. Start the Inspiration Age in the late middle ages or the very start of the early modern period.<br /> <br /> Picture Elizabeth I as a Stalwart. John Dee could be a Mesmerist. Oh how could you list the Daredevils?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's slightly earlier than the era I was imagining (I was thinking Restoration rather than Elizabethan) but I do think a Swashbuckling historic era is a must! Call it &quot;Allez&quot;!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T09:52:10-08:00","id":1191644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191635#post1191635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Continuum allows for alternate timelines. A Multiverse would allow for alternate <i>realities</i>, with differences too drastic even for the Butterfly Effect to account for. For instance, a universe where the other planets in the Solar System are habitable, or where there's a vast galactic community of aliens (instead of aliens being rare and either ding off or transcending after \u201conly\u201d 10,000 years). Or where Earth is populated by anthropomorphic animals instead of humans. Or where the gods of myth are <i>real</i>, and coexist with humanity as it expands to the stars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You may be underestimating the reality-editing power of Z-rays.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T16:19:21-08:00","id":1191770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191640#post1191640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's slightly earlier than the era I was imagining (I was thinking Restoration rather than Elizabethan) but I do think a Swashbuckling historic era is a must! Call it &quot;Allez&quot;!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not Allez. Try Athanor, an alchemical furness used to speed transformations. Or some other alchemy themed name. This would both connect the setting to the theme of transformation and discovery, profoundly appropriate to the early modern period, and give a nod to where the PCs would think their Inspiration comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-04-2018, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T18:20:55-08:00","id":1191793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191770#post1191770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not Allez. Try Athanor, an alchemical furness used to speed transformations. Or some other alchemy themed name. This would both connect the setting to the theme of transformation and discovery, profoundly appropriate to the early modern period, and give a nod to where the PCs would think their Inspiration comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Athanor works!<br /> <br /> My other major idea for a pre-Adventure! setting potentially in the same timeline (other than Aegis, which of course is actually happening, so CALLED IT!) was Abnatural - which would be in the Victorian Age, include Mesmerist spiritualism, Gothic science, and related paranormal horror.<br /> <br /> (there was also Atomic, set in the 1950s, but that's so close to &quot;They From Beneath the Sea!&quot; that it seems less feasible now... then again the concept for Aegis is pretty close to Scion)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-04-2018, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T18:50:21-08:00","id":1191797,"title":"","content":"Tinkering with my &quot;Edwardian Psions&quot; setting (where the War of Worlds invasion happened in the 1890s, and the left over alien tech leads to the psion age in a pseudo-steam-punk-ish setting)... and who has what Promethean Chamber. I think one of the conceits of this setting is that pools of Latents come from exposure to certain alien tech fallout, so in some cases a given empire is reliant on pulling largely, though never completely, from certain regions for their Psions.<br /> <br /> The British Empire has the Biokinesis Chamber - but the largest pool of Latents in the Empire are Indian, which leads to issues as you can imagine.<br /> <br /> The German Empire has the Psychokinesis Chamber<br /> <br /> The US has two Chambers, but neither wholly under the control of the government. A New England spiritualist cult has the Clairsentience Chamber, and Tesla built the Electrokinesis Chamber in Colorado Springs<br /> <br /> An international Leftist underground has the Teleporter Chamber<br /> <br /> The Empire of Japan has the Vitakinetic Chamber (it\u2019s a few decades early compared to real history, but I chose this because of Raiki\u2019s creation in the 1920s).<br /> <br /> China takes the role of Nippon in the normal Aeon setting - in the wake of the alien invasion, the Boxers were victorious in seizing control of China which has now gone harshly isolationist, and true to theme of the &quot;Fists of Harmony and Justice&quot; they use the left over alien tech to create Superiors rather than Psions.<br /> <br /> I haven't decided yet on the Telepathy Chamber, and I'm not sure whether this setting will even include the Quantakinesis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-05-2018, 02:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T10:53:24-08:00","id":1191994,"title":"","content":"The Dervish State has the Telepathy Chamber, their Order weaving telepathy together with Sufi mysticism and unity through faith - and they're quickly rising to turn the Ottoman Empire into THEIR client state!<br /> <br /> Quantakinetics doesn't exist in this setting YET, but the French government has entrused as much scavenged alien Psi tech as they can find to Marie Curie to see what she can come up with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T23:13:47-08:00","id":1194146,"title":"","content":"As I prepare this game I've come up with an interesting scenario in the background of the game.<br /> <br /> For [reasons] I've included a thread of the campaign that involves Anteus and his departure from Project utopia to pursue his own agenda as an environmental activist/terrorist.<br /> <br /> As part of the campaign, Anteus learns about the multi-verse. This throws him into a significant moral quandry. Is his environmental obligations simply to the earth he inhabits? to ll earths? to the abstract concept of natural dominance?<br /> <br /> It throws him into a bit of an anguished state and sets him on the hunt for the dimension hopping nova that has entered the game-universe to learn more about the nature of the multi-verse, and thus he ends up in opposition with the PCs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Visit me at <a href=\"http://www.bragrman.com\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Tales of Grey</i></a> - my RPG Game-Master's blog.<br /> <br /> &quot;If only I had an enemy bigger than my apathy, I could have won&quot; - <i>I gave you all,</i> Mumford &amp; Sons","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8520-capitantypo","name":"CapitanTypo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8520_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"896"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T01:27:26-07:00","id":1196739,"title":"","content":"Been meaning to post more updates on my Multiverse idea.<br /> <br /> So the change happens with the Hammerspace Incident. Basically when its activated it ties three universes together in that in one Universe only Bhurano Survives out of the three closest to the explosion, in another only Donighal, and in another Mercer. But Mercer is able to communicate with the other two. They decide to form an Aeon Society Trinity. They pool their information because their universes are identical, at least at first. So they can start gathering information and those who can harness Telluric Energies. They realize if they can gather information in one universe it can be shared among the other ones, and there they would be secret knowledge. They make plans, not only do they assemble the Talents of the world they agree to explore different aspects of the world and share it among the highest echelons of the Aeon Society. So if one universe, say Donighals explores secret areas of the ocean they can discover ruins and natural wonders and the other two universes will know of the findings without having to expend the resources themselves. If Bhurano's society discovers a Gold mine or Petroleum deposit then the other universe know where they are without having to tip their hand with excavations. They also realize their Universe are quickly diverging. The next generation of people born are not guaranteed to be born in all three Universes, but they also discover some interesting individuals called Constants or Coins who exist in two or more Universes even with all the strange changes in all unlikeliness they are still always born. This individuals often become Talents, or later Aberrants or Psions.<br /> <br /> So they start sharing information which funds their society, including development of technology. If they truly need to early on in the history of the group they can even do things such as befriend individuals in one universe to gain things such as secret personal information so they can rob or ruin them in another universe. They also decide to essentially plagiarizer Artists and Authors in one Universe to benefit from it in the other two. Thus the Aeon Society is a strange source of prolific poetry, classical literature and groundbreaking science. This is a distasteful and disagreeable tactic at first but they put in their charter the concept of repaying Constants/Coins they discover if any of the other universes has record of benefiting from their counterparts, so they take the opportunity to give them donations or even have them taken care of and educated.<br /> <br /> Eventually Bhurano becomes the Authority on Quantum and Noetics. She starts developing a plan to cultivate Psi in her Universe, while Donighal now Doctor Primoris plans to back Quantum as the destiny of his World and works on creating Novas. Mercer works with Primoris to Create a Gate on the Moon of Primoris' Universe that can send Primoris and a cadre of his emergent Novas into Mercers Universe. They secretly build a Moon Portal in Mercers Universe and eventually create a Trinity of Gateways in each Universe and are finally able to travel across the Universes with great effort and resources. They can now finally fully trade in resources if they have to, but even more importantly staff. Now they develop a level of Clearance in the Aeon Society that represents not only knowing of the Multiverse but also knowing they can travel between them. They work on making easier travel from the Earth to the Moon, the Aeon Society is easily a Hundred Years ahead of the rest of the world in this regard, and in many other aspects of medicine and science as well.<br /> <br /> Soon they realize the nature of Quantum and Noetics, and how Noetics seems to dampen and stiffle Quantum. Primoris and Bhurano come to an agreement they would smuggle as many of the Mesmers and Psiads of his Universe into her own as the Novas become more and more prominent. At first its only a handful of Novas starting in 60's but enough to develop decent super science, and Stalwarts kept on erupting, though at a lesser rate then the age of Adventure. While Bhurano also has Mesmers appear in her universe with extra refugees from Primoris's world. She develops technologies which cultivate mesmers, and eventually Psiads, while at the same time Stalwarts become rarer and rarer, and only a handful of Novas exist (each from a unique anomaly such as Alien Interference and experimental Gamma Bombs). She lays the groundwork for a method to uplift humans into something she calls Psions.<br /> <br /> Eventually Primoris has a Falling out with the Trinity. He wishes to create an event which will lead to worldwide Eruptions of Novas. He eventually follows through with this and also departs the Aeon Trinity. He spends over a decade gathering Nova followers, secretly his group has discovered their is a 4th Universe where they all died during the Hammersmith Incident and he secretly departs for it. In this Universe he is Divis Mal, and his discoveries from the Shared Aeon Trinity put him at a significant advantage in this Universe. Because this is a Universe without an Aeon Society it has had a more natural evolution of technology and thus he is secretly unrivaled in his access to knowledge and technology. He sets himself up as Emperor as creates a worldwide Erruption event. He plans to find a way to discover and conquer Universes beyond the Trinity (Plus his 4th Universe Universe Zero/Null). And makes plan to also conquer the Trinity as that is at first the only universes he can travel too. Though he creates his Trinity Gates on a secret Base deep in below the Surface of Mars on all 4 Universes, as its far enough away that he could hide from the Aeon Society as they would be the only ones able to theoretically travel to Mars, but only at great cost.<br /> <br /> By the default starting date 2028 Bhurano's Universe has just finished her Amrita Serum which when given to an individual known as a latent and put through a Soma Chamber she has created Psions. Bhuranoverse has a world with a much greater degree of Medical/Genetic science. The Primorium (Divis Mal's original Universe) is generally in a worse condition then the other two universes of the Trinity due to losing their Stewart, and actually a lot of the problems is because of the Conflict and sabotage when Divis Mal left. Mercer and Bhurano's factions have somewhat exploited this universe as it is not their own. Super Villains imperil the world, and the Doyen have been made aware of this world ahead of the others and make plans to figure out how to handle the Earth, and when they discover the Trinity Gate phenomena they panic and get desperate...<br /> <br /> Max Mercer's Continuum is more hands off, which has resulted in a world of Talents. His world is over all the most advanced of the Continuum as his method has been to shepard and uplift humanity as a whole. But talented squads of Psions/Psiads are found here. Many are secretly stationed in this universe but outside of the Aeon Society the world thinks the Psions are some miracles of the Aeon Society, ignorant of the Multiverse.<br /> <br /> Eventually the Aeon Society will have defend against Divis Mal's Worldbreaker Dynasty and the Doyen first of the Primorium, but depending on how that war goes they may make plans against the other Doyen or if they defeat the Primorium Doyen their survivors unite the Bhuranoverse and Continuum Doyen.<br /> <br /> Yes once I get revised Aberrant Rules this is probably the first chronicle I would like to try for Aeon! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-18T03:28:53-07:00","id":1196759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1191797#post1191797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Cool stoof!</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh I like this! Maybe instead of Fallout latents come from some sort of alien retrovirus, so while we defeated the martians with germs their germs are uplifting us.<br /> <br /> The thing is we need a reason for why we only have one chamber each and they are so equally distributed. So maybe it they were salvaged from the Invaders mothership and science Vessel. So maybe the Psychokineses, Electrokineses, and Teleporter chambers were part of the great military engines on the mother ship, and Vita and Bio were in the Science vessel, and the others were bought/stolen/salvaged on the black market by the other nations?<br /> <br /> So a question I had even with War of the Worlds, wouldn't this mean that Mars still poses a threat? Maybe they are in a state of upheaval with a plague but they are still probably around?<br /> <br /> And maybe the Martians experimented on Humans quantum potential and created a handful of Aberrants: Eugene Sandow as with Enhanced strength, a Preteen Einstein endowed with Enhanced intellect, and a young Gandhi with... plasma breath...<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T16:42:01-07:00","id":1197387,"title":"","content":"Question pertaining to alternate timelines and all that. Max Mercer is a time traveller, but I don't know what that means... I know he is long lived but it keeps being brought up that he is a time traveller. I know its some sort of Flux power, probably the high version of Talent?<br /> <br /> And does time travel create new timelines rather then alter the world? So Mecer is just hoping between parallel universes, but some of these universes are ahead or behind his default one? What?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-19T18:53:53-07:00","id":1197434,"title":"","content":"We don\u2019t know yet exactly how other timelines are actually going to play out in Trinity Core canon, only that they are a thing. I would strongly suspect one of the unrevealed \u201ceras\u201d will focus on playing Tier 3 Paramorphs (of which Max was the first, but not last) and explore time travel and alternate timelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T19:59:39-07:00","id":1198518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1197434#post1197434\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We don\u2019t know yet exactly how other timelines are actually going to play out in Trinity Core canon, only that they are a thing. I would strongly suspect one of the unrevealed \u201ceras\u201d will focus on playing Tier 3 Paramorphs (of which Max was the first, but not last) and explore time travel and alternate timelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I suspect Quantum Leap/Journeyman style game is eventually going to be created.<br /> <br /> But how did we know Mercer could time travel? I see the wiki explains the history of his time traveling going to the future then returning to the time he left and possibly faking being his own son. Was it in a fiction section that talks about him time traveling?<br /> <br /> The wiki seems to indicate to me timetravel doesn't alter reality, nor does it go into another universe (at least not always). Mercer seemed to actually travel into the future and return to his own time, and everything he did wasn't contradicted and seemed to be something destined to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:25:03-07:00","id":1198529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1198518#post1198518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The wiki seems to indicate to me timetravel doesn't alter reality, nor does it go into another universe (at least not always). Mercer seemed to actually travel into the future and return to his own time, and everything he did wasn't contradicted and seemed to be something destined to happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the previous edition didn't have shifting timelines, and this one does, so I wouldn't make too many assumptions on the previous edition. IIRC Mercer's bouncing in time is hinted at through his appereances in the Aeon era, and then discussed more in-depthly in the Adventure! book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:35:39-07:00","id":1198532,"title":"","content":"So we don't have any description of him using his time powers, only descriptions of evidence that the power was used? So we don't know if say he teleports himself, or even creates a portal, or it is an unwilling shift?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T20:42:23-07:00","id":1198536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1198532#post1198532\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So we don't have any description of him using his time powers, only descriptions of evidence that the power was used? So we don't know if say he teleports himself, or even creates a portal, or it is an unwilling shift?</div> </div> </div> </div>There's some indication it may be unwilling - but no the power is never detailed explicitly.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of having characters encounter a Max Mercer who doesn't have control of when he'll shift, and so mostly just hands off information for others to do good with, or ties to learn as much as he can to use after his next shift - but also sometimes meet a more zen Max that appears to have perfect awareness of his movement in time (if not true control, his perspective of causality may have lifted the illusion of control...) and is more enigmatic and less direct in his interventions.<br /> <br /> The reason for the difference of course, is they're encountering Max at different points in his own timeline out of order. Bouncing around out of control just trying to hand off information to do as much good as possible Max is earlier (Tier 3 paramorph). Buddha of Time Max is after he finally makes peace with his relationship with time and achieves understanding of his own causality (Tier 4 paramorph).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:10:56-07:00","id":1198548,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a Trinity Multiverse game where the entire Multiverse has collapsed as a result of tinkering in time by other Nova's throughout multiple Earths. The current run of the campaign is on a solitary Earth that was created by a dying Nova on the old Prime Earth, it has none of the trappings of the metaplot - but the PC's found a means to travel to the dead prime Earth - eventually they'll find their way to the Earths in the multiverse where the timeline has been rebooted (I.E. a transition campaign to say goodbye to first edition and create an in-narrative reason to reboot some of our old favorite characters into the new Continuum version of the system when it comes out)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:17:21-07:00","id":1198550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dirtypoolfilms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1198548#post1198548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm currently running a Trinity Multiverse game where the entire Multiverse has collapsed as a result of tinkering in time by other Nova's throughout multiple Earths. The current run of the campaign is on a solitary Earth that was created by a dying Nova on the old Prime Earth, it has none of the trappings of the metaplot - but the PC's found a means to travel to the dead prime Earth - eventually they'll find their way to the Earths in the multiverse where the timeline has been rebooted (I.E. a transition campaign to say goodbye to first edition and create an in-narrative reason to reboot some of our old favorite characters into the new Continuum version of the system when it comes out)</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty cool. I've had similar ideas for Mage and Exalted based off the patchwork Battleworld concept from Marvel. Mage where the different Horizon realms and Worlds created by Archmages were shattered by the Reckoning and Avatar Storm so one being grapped handfuls of different shattered worlds and smashed them together. With Exalted it was pocket Creations that were lost during the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> So yeah I like the idea of both Time and Universes being damaged and collapsing. And I would like a setting with a mishmash from different eras and alternate timelines being something like a Patchwork Earth saved from a Collapsed Multiverse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-22T21:30:14-07:00","id":1198553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1198550#post1198550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's pretty cool. I've had similar ideas for Mage and Exalted based off the patchwork Battleworld concept from Marvel. Mage where the different Horizon realms and Worlds created by Archmages were shattered by the Reckoning and Avatar Storm so one being grapped handfuls of different shattered worlds and smashed them together. With Exalted it was pocket Creations that were lost during the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> So yeah I like the idea of both Time and Universes being damaged and collapsing. And I would like a setting with a mishmash from different eras and alternate timelines being something like a Patchwork Earth saved from a Collapsed Multiverse.</div> </div> </div> </div>My setting is actually a complex Multiverse that comprises all the White Wolf product lines where Creation splintered and fractured after the return of The Scarlett Empress, the result is an infinite cosmological omniverse where each game line exists as its own Multiverse. For added flavor, it goes deeper still, so that somewhere in my Multiverse - your campaigns exist on their own world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23889-dirtypoolfilms","name":"dirtypoolfilms","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T11:31:42-07:00","id":1198773,"title":"","content":"In the year where in standard Aberrant history Divis Mal releases the Null Manifesto in this one he basically uses his awe inspiring presence to call the Novas, governments of the world, and Aeon Society together for a massive Convocation. Which after some time comes up with an Accord to balance the nova being with baseline society. <br /> <br /> This Accord doesn't create a Nova run world but rather finds a way for both to work together and balance each other so neither group looses out. <br /> <br /> Over time the Accords create a planetary government, maybe as an outgrowth of the UN maybe not, where novas sacrifice some of their time for the greater good in order to allow greater humanity more hope and unity. Humanity, in exchange, sacrifices their full on power over Novas to also gain the fruits of nova ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T12:53:44-07:00","id":1198811,"title":"","content":"I'm currently running a game where Process 418 lead to the colapse of time. Through the current game the players will learn of the 1e time line, and the efforts that allowed the current 2e time line to exists. They will then have to stop a new iteration of the experiement that caused 418 from irreparably colapsing the new timeline and possibly all of existance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-23T19:30:52-07:00","id":1198935,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking on Hammersmith himself and how I hope they tap his character for some future Era. Like maybe his mind was shunted quantum leap style.<br /> <br /> In my Multiverse Campaign I will Tie him probably to the Universe Zero where neither Bhurano, Donighal, or Mercer survived.<br /> <br /> <br /> But thinking on the high Quantum Universe Creation, maybe its a simpler Universe at first and one would need other Nova's to help flesh it out. So it could be more an act of a Pantheon of Novas lead by a Chieftain rather then one supreme god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-26T00:55:12-07:00","id":1199625,"title":"","content":"Listening to the Futurist Isaac Arthur has filled me with a lot idea. But I am going back to the Multiverse Portals idea. So going back to Divis Mal's World Breaker concept were he plunders the Multiverse I wonder how much his homebase of Universe Zero/Null could support from plundered resources from multiple other worlds. If the portal is on Earth then you wouldn't need to expend the resources to go back and forth from the Sun. And how Fusion generators would just totally change the world.<br /> <br /> Some crazy ideas could be maybe Divis Mal could even steal one or more moons to create an artificial nearby earthlike planet as a vault of items. Or maybe with mars, stealing enough mass to make it more Earth like.<br /> <br /> Or stealing the Oceans of another Earth, like that episode of SWAT Kats.<br /> <br /> And then Slaves, if Divis Mal plunders worlds for slaves that would be an essential endless wave of disposable labor, but that probably isn't Divis's style unless he goes all Homo Superior on mankind.<br /> <br /> Or more experimental he has Universe Zero as his home base and doesn't mess with things to crazily, but could experiment on other universes like smashing together smaller bodies to create Earth sized planets, or even experimenting with Exploding a Sun to see if he can make a more supreme Quantum Wave many times greater then the Hammersmith Event, but would essentially destroy a Solar System, but perhaps he can shield the Earth enough where he can let people survive long enough to erupt, and then he can abandoned the rest to die.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:04:14-07:00","id":1200170,"title":"","content":"Using the whole humans going/building a dyson sphere led me to this idea.<br /> <br /> Basically in the modern day Earth there is an Inspired scientist who announces the establishment of a project to build a rocket carrier designed to serve as a method of transport for a collection of scientists, explorers, and colonists to a new world beyond Earth's solar system. Some of the lowkey funding for this operation is done by the Aeon Society, though that is more of a nod nod wink wink.<br /> <br /> The rocket carrier is populated by say a few thousand people in suspension - which uses Inspired developed technology - and blasts off as predicted. Something happens, an explosion occurs on the quantum level and the rocket is lost, believed to be destroyed. Earth gets bathed in quantum energies and untold numbers of novas appear.Of course that is just a bit of side information, not the major point of the campaign. <br /> <br /> The ship itself survived the explosion, and being bathed in the Telluric (which I know isn't its own energy but its a good word to describe how the ship got hit by both quantum and subquantum/noetic energy( and actually began traveling through a warp tunnel/ Hours, maybe a day or so later, it came out in the orbit of a dyson sphere, though it quickly lost orbit and crashed on the planet. Thanks to the Inspired sciences that were part of its design it survived more or less intact, though its engines are damaged to unusability. Once matters stabilize the command crew wakes up the first-in crew (which is the PCs) and operations are launched to try and figure out what is going on in this alien world. Thankfully the Inspired scientist is still around and whole he declares he doesn't have the resources to rebuild the ship he can, if given proper materials, create new and innovative tools and equipment and even buildings. <br /> <br /> In time the PCs, and the command crew and any colonists that are awaken, all begin to exhibit signs of change,of awakenings. This will lead to the formations of Talents, Stalwarts, and Mesmerists - though names can be changed as needed with the note that eventually some will become Novas and Psiads. <br /> <br /> The campaign is exploration and survey at first, but also can contain resource gathering and society building since the few thousand people in suspension need a place to live and work when awoken. Thankfully the dyson sphere they landed on has a Earth like atmosphere and copious amounts of plant and animal life, as well as numerous other mysterious - like who built it and where are they now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":661,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","user":"LordHeru","date":". 03-27-2018, 03:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T12:31:17-07:00","id":1200183,"title":"","content":"Did they accidentally go into a Wormhole into a Parallel World?<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm the colonists idea has me thinking, what about working on a time machine project, secret well funded emergency project to save America as a famine rages from Quantum taint plaguing the farmbelt of the continent. They accidentally discover Time Travel was beyond them but accidentally created a Wormhole into a parallel Earth, one where the planet seems somewhat staggered millions of years behind. The Secret Project Odysseus realizes they can't afford to ignore this opportunity, while they can't travel back in time to save America, they can create a Colony in this primitive Thunder Lizard festooned World to grow food, and harness resources to save America before it falls into its 2nd Civil War and conquers Mexico and Canada.<br /> <br /> I could even tie this into my Trinity Multiverse campaign idea. Maybe as the first World that Divis Mal figured out how to stumble upon, due to the Worlds Flux caused by Wormhole making it easier to enter/discover by Divis Mal's Worldbreakers.<br /> <br /> Maybe going through the Wormhole into Pangaea has a tendency to spawn talents among the crew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-27T14:17:39-07:00","id":1200225,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar754_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"754\" data-vbnamecard=\"754\">Eldagusto</a> Though I wasn't really going the direction of a wormhole to a parallel world, more that the wormhole is how the FTL tech work. (Maybe call it the Telluric Engine, for funzies) <br /> <br /> I have to admit your idea is brilliant as well and, is in fact, a campaign idea that I have long liked and enjoyed - both the variety with actual time travel (that is its a prehistoric Earth in a parallel line) and without (its another world with a surprisingly Earth like environment for reasons that are hard to explain). The idea of it being the one last attempt to survive or to keep the culture going or to [insert special need here] is an intriguing one to me. As are the idea that the people brought over <br /> <br /> One of the things that I liked about my rocket carrier idea was that because the colonists are in suspended animation at the start it can be up to the players when they awaken - which means they start with them being one of the few and as the campaign progresses they become the elite in a growing and developing civilization on an unknown world or space artifact or something edgy. <br /> <br /> One of the actual Aberrant rpg campaigns I ran was just that - Divis Mal (using a pseudonym) sponsored a stargate-like project to explore and chart worlds. The worlds were parallel, because there is something fun in exploring a fantasy Rome with tanks and a such. <br /> <br /> I LOVE (LOVE LOVE) the idea that human interplanetary and/or interstellar exploration and colonization leads to the appearance of first Talents and then the other Inspired and then full versions of them later on, first on the project members and then later on among all of humanity. So yeah, whether its humans colonizing Mars, or humans colonizing a parallel world, or humans colonizing a dyson sphere in the end said humans will go from purely baseline to mixed baseline and Inspired to eventually all Inspired, because I consider that AWESOME! <br /> <br /> Heck, when I read Trinity all those years ago and they mentioned Eden, and then when Stellar Frontier came out, my mind went to &quot;I want to be those pioneers who first settled Eden and worlds like it, I WANT THAT CAMPAIGN!!! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-28T06:46:55-07:00","id":1200408,"title":"","content":"Oh I think my confusion lies in thinking this was only a thread on traveling between Universes, but it seems to have expanded to include Parallel Universes/Timelines in general without the transportation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-30T08:44:17-07:00","id":1201285,"title":"","content":"I'm a fan of the Marvel comic Exiles from a decade back. The idea was a group composed of alternate reality superheroes plucked from their timelines due to multiversal irregularities and them performing missions in different realities to fix the knot in the multiverse to make their home realities viable again. Their missions could range from stopping just one bank robbery to freeing the human race enslave by the Skrulls for the last Century so they could fight off Galactus.<br /> <br /> This in itself could be inspiration for a setting, reality hopping Heroes. But even if not it raises some interesting notions and character potentials. Like what about encountering a Donighal from another Reality where he became a Psiad instead of a Nova/Stalwart? Or bringing in full on characters from Comic Books like a Symbiote possessed Peter Parker? We know other realities exist that don't follow the same laws of Trinity Universe. It could be in another Universe you don't have Quantum and Psi like normal and you have Mutants instead? It could be interesting to introduce Psychics and Supermen who don't follow the same rules as exactly as Novas and Psions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T12:07:43-07:00","id":1212740,"title":"","content":"I was just thinking of how there are often prohibitions on messing with time. But what of we went the opposite. <br /> <br /> So let's say the game starts on a variant nova or psion age Earth (both are possible depending what people want) where things are bad. Like very very bad. Like one cannot breath in the environment and most animal and plant life are dead and we live in sealed domes in the ruins of civilization past. <br /> <br /> Then someone comes up with time travel technology and the computational ability to map out parts of the timestream, lay out futures, and such. Following this a plan is put into operation to change history in order to bring about a better, more glorious future. <br /> <br /> The way this would work is a team, hint hint, of agents will go back in time to particular focal points. There they make certain changes - some narrow, some simple, some broad, some complex - which over time and a sequence of trips will change the whole of history. Thus bringing about a better present and future. <br /> <br /> Obviously difficulties and dangers would arise, maybe a conflict with a mysterious group doing the same thing, etc. <br /> <br /> Taking ideas from other sources something about the technology means the complex and those in it remember both worlds even as the greater world doesn't. <br /> <br /> I think at first stinking thing to past history could be right but then suddenly something unique is discovered and scientists realize they can actually make use of parallel worlds and alternate timelines in their vast timeline planning. <br /> <br /> Do you really want it so dinosaurs never died put and in the present day they are much of our beast of burden. <br /> <br /> Or how about do you really think it's right to have novas/psions(psiads) be present from dawn of history. <br /> <br /> The cool thing is that the players get to basically design the past history of this new world they are forming. Of course using the options the ST provide.<br /> <br /> Thoughts anyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:16:15-07:00","id":1212924,"title":"","content":"Are they changing their own world or changing another world's past? How do you explain the characters not changing with the universe, or the fact that if they did change it then they wouldn't be able to go back in time? Why is the world by default doomsdayed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-04-28T21:40:05-07:00","id":1212930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1212924#post1212924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are they changing their own world or changing another world's past? How do you explain the characters not changing with the universe, or the fact that if they did change it then they wouldn't be able to go back in time? Why is the world by default doomsdayed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think they are changing there own worlds past. Basically after a bunch of focused changes the world will change. <br /> <br /> The science they ate using eventually let's them add parts of other timelines to tere own history, thus making things different. <br /> <br /> The device (noetic or quantum) creates a resonate effect that protects the time travelers and those within a certain range of it as well. They remember the old world and they slot fully into the new one with no issue. <br /> <br /> On the last one, game fiat. Unless things get changed then destruction is expected. <br /> <br /> I do think that not all time and dimension travel leads to changes to the world's timeline, only certain specific changes do. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the comment. I kind of think this is fun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T13:42:04-07:00","id":1213877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1212930#post1212930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The device (noetic or quantum) creates a resonate effect that protects the time travelers and those within a certain range of it as well. They remember the old world and they slot fully into the new one with no issue.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love the idea of the bubble and the explicit understanding that if they ever return to their chronological time (i.e. 2020 or whatever) that it's borderline impossible that anyone they know could have possibly ever been born. BUT maybe things get really, really weird and they return to their own era and there are original versions of themselves there. Perhaps ones without powers or maybe they're villains. Could really be a really fun setting. Especially to introduce Talents into worlds with either Psions, Psiots, Novas or super-tech. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T15:38:18-07:00","id":1213924,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty cool idea that they come back to their time and there are rival versions of them now. Also if the secret that time travel is a thing has been going on I would imagine a lot of people would view them as genocidal madmen since they essentially erased whole generations from existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-01T19:15:17-07:00","id":1214011,"title":"","content":"See in this setting the world is dying, nearly dead, most of humanity lays huddled in one or a few of the surviving domes.<br /> <br /> In an attempt to find some way for humanity to go on an Inspired scientist discovered the time travel technology. This method of temporal alteration is the only way for humanity to survive in this setting. <br /> <br /> Maybe once they push start on the alterations time travel becomes more restricted then it used to be. <br /> <br /> The thing is I do not want to one into this setting with the thought or concept that what there doing is bad. The whole concept is change the past to make a future worth living in. <br /> <br /> The idea of going to worlds and finding alternate selves could work, when they go the more world variant routes. <br /> <br /> I think the world doesn't flow into a new past until a techno-telluric ritual gets activated. Then in a whoosh existence rearranges around the domes so that a whole different past exists leading to a world much more glorious then it was. <br /> <br /> So those who survived the destruction remain, with memories, but now so do billions of others. Billions who died in a vast series of apocalyptic wars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T01:46:41-08:00","id":1290692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1196739#post1196739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Been meaning to post more updates on my Multiverse idea.<br /> <br /> So the change happens with the Hammerspace Incident. Basically when its activated it ties three universes together in that in one Universe only Bhurano Survives out of the three closest to the explosion, in another only Donighal, and in another Mercer. But Mercer is able to communicate with the other two. They decide to form an Aeon Society Trinity. They pool their information because their universes are identical, at least at first. So they can start gathering information and those who can harness Telluric Energies. They realize if they can gather information in one universe it can be shared among the other ones, and there they would be secret knowledge. They make plans, not only do they assemble the Talents of the world they agree to explore different aspects of the world and share it among the highest echelons of the Aeon Society. So if one universe, say Donighals explores secret areas of the ocean they can discover ruins and natural wonders and the other two universes will know of the findings without having to expend the resources themselves. If Bhurano's society discovers a Gold mine or Petroleum deposit then the other universe know where they are without having to tip their hand with excavations. They also realize their Universe are quickly diverging. The next generation of people born are not guaranteed to be born in all three Universes, but they also discover some interesting individuals called Constants or Coins who exist in two or more Universes even with all the strange changes in all unlikeliness they are still always born. This individuals often become Talents, or later Aberrants or Psions.<br /> <br /> So they start sharing information which funds their society, including development of technology. If they truly need to early on in the history of the group they can even do things such as befriend individuals in one universe to gain things such as secret personal information so they can rob or ruin them in another universe. They also decide to essentially plagiarizer Artists and Authors in one Universe to benefit from it in the other two. Thus the Aeon Society is a strange source of prolific poetry, classical literature and groundbreaking science. This is a distasteful and disagreeable tactic at first but they put in their charter the concept of repaying Constants/Coins they discover if any of the other universes has record of benefiting from their counterparts, so they take the opportunity to give them donations or even have them taken care of and educated.<br /> <br /> Eventually Bhurano becomes the Authority on Quantum and Noetics. She starts developing a plan to cultivate Psi in her Universe, while Donighal now Doctor Primoris plans to back Quantum as the destiny of his World and works on creating Novas. Mercer works with Primoris to Create a Gate on the Moon of Primoris' Universe that can send Primoris and a cadre of his emergent Novas into Mercers Universe. They secretly build a Moon Portal in Mercers Universe and eventually create a Trinity of Gateways in each Universe and are finally able to travel across the Universes with great effort and resources. They can now finally fully trade in resources if they have to, but even more importantly staff. Now they develop a level of Clearance in the Aeon Society that represents not only knowing of the Multiverse but also knowing they can travel between them. They work on making easier travel from the Earth to the Moon, the Aeon Society is easily a Hundred Years ahead of the rest of the world in this regard, and in many other aspects of medicine and science as well.<br /> <br /> Soon they realize the nature of Quantum and Noetics, and how Noetics seems to dampen and stiffle Quantum. Primoris and Bhurano come to an agreement they would smuggle as many of the Mesmers and Psiads of his Universe into her own as the Novas become more and more prominent. At first its only a handful of Novas starting in 60's but enough to develop decent super science, and Stalwarts kept on erupting, though at a lesser rate then the age of Adventure. While Bhurano also has Mesmers appear in her universe with extra refugees from Primoris's world. She develops technologies which cultivate mesmers, and eventually Psiads, while at the same time Stalwarts become rarer and rarer, and only a handful of Novas exist (each from a unique anomaly such as Alien Interference and experimental Gamma Bombs). She lays the groundwork for a method to uplift humans into something she calls Psions.<br /> <br /> Eventually Primoris has a Falling out with the Trinity. He wishes to create an event which will lead to worldwide Eruptions of Novas. He eventually follows through with this and also departs the Aeon Trinity. He spends over a decade gathering Nova followers, secretly his group has discovered their is a 4th Universe where they all died during the Hammersmith Incident and he secretly departs for it. In this Universe he is Divis Mal, and his discoveries from the Shared Aeon Trinity put him at a significant advantage in this Universe. Because this is a Universe without an Aeon Society it has had a more natural evolution of technology and thus he is secretly unrivaled in his access to knowledge and technology. He sets himself up as Emperor as creates a worldwide Erruption event. He plans to find a way to discover and conquer Universes beyond the Trinity (Plus his 4th Universe Universe Zero/Null). And makes plan to also conquer the Trinity as that is at first the only universes he can travel too. Though he creates his Trinity Gates on a secret Base deep in below the Surface of Mars on all 4 Universes, as its far enough away that he could hide from the Aeon Society as they would be the only ones able to theoretically travel to Mars, but only at great cost.<br /> <br /> By the default starting date 2028 Bhurano's Universe has just finished her Amrita Serum which when given to an individual known as a latent and put through a Soma Chamber she has created Psions. Bhuranoverse has a world with a much greater degree of Medical/Genetic science. The Primorium (Divis Mal's original Universe) is generally in a worse condition then the other two universes of the Trinity due to losing their Stewart, and actually a lot of the problems is because of the Conflict and sabotage when Divis Mal left. Mercer and Bhurano's factions have somewhat exploited this universe as it is not their own. Super Villains imperil the world, and the Doyen have been made aware of this world ahead of the others and make plans to figure out how to handle the Earth, and when they discover the Trinity Gate phenomena they panic and get desperate...<br /> <br /> Max Mercer's Continuum is more hands off, which has resulted in a world of Talents. His world is over all the most advanced of the Continuum as his method has been to shepard and uplift humanity as a whole. But talented squads of Psions/Psiads are found here. Many are secretly stationed in this universe but outside of the Aeon Society the world thinks the Psions are some miracles of the Aeon Society, ignorant of the Multiverse.<br /> <br /> Eventually the Aeon Society will have defend against Divis Mal's Worldbreaker Dynasty and the Doyen first of the Primorium, but depending on how that war goes they may make plans against the other Doyen or if they defeat the Primorium Doyen their survivors unite the Bhuranoverse and Continuum Doyen.<br /> <br /> Yes once I get revised Aberrant Rules this is probably the first chronicle I would like to try for Aeon! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1199625#post1199625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Listening to the Futurist Isaac Arthur has filled me with a lot idea. But I am going back to the Multiverse Portals idea. So going back to Divis Mal's World Breaker concept were he plunders the Multiverse I wonder how much his homebase of Universe Zero/Null could support from plundered resources from multiple other worlds. If the portal is on Earth then you wouldn't need to expend the resources to go back and forth from the Sun. And how Fusion generators would just totally change the world.<br /> <br /> Some crazy ideas could be maybe Divis Mal could even steal one or more moons to create an artificial nearby earthlike planet as a vault of items. Or maybe with mars, stealing enough mass to make it more Earth like.<br /> <br /> Or stealing the Oceans of another Earth, like that episode of SWAT Kats.<br /> <br /> And then Slaves, if Divis Mal plunders worlds for slaves that would be an essential endless wave of disposable labor, but that probably isn't Divis's style unless he goes all Homo Superior on mankind.<br /> <br /> Or more experimental he has Universe Zero as his home base and doesn't mess with things to crazily, but could experiment on other universes like smashing together smaller bodies to create Earth sized planets, or even experimenting with Exploding a Sun to see if he can make a more supreme Quantum Wave many times greater then the Hammersmith Event, but would essentially destroy a Solar System, but perhaps he can shield the Earth enough where he can let people survive long enough to erupt, and then he can abandoned the rest to die.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay bumping this thread and quoting myself so I can gather my notes.<br /> <br /> Ideas I\u2019ve refined:<br /> <br /> The Trinity Continuum is the Umbrella group, like Pentex and it\u2019s subsidiaries, for the Early Mercer, Bhurano, and Donighal. It is a way for them all to have a say as a tribunal council type of arrangement.<br /> <br /> Aeon is Mercer\u2019s Universe and Mercer Founds the the Aeon Society as his Branch of the Trinity. His Universe is laissez faire though they discouraged Quantum and a lot of their Noetically inclined Individuals go to work for Bhurano\u2019s Soma Universe. So mostly Talents in this Universe<br /> <br /> Bhurano\u2019s Universe is the Noetia, and her branch of Trinity is the Soma Institute for Noetic affairs (though I considered also a name like Amrita Corp and such or just the Noetic Institute or Bhurano Industries or Corp or Tech). Bhurano worked to Nullify Quantum, especially as she discovered the Madness and ego in Primoris\u2019 Primorium. The concentration of Psi users gather from the other Universe chain reacts creating more and more Psi and less and less Quantum.<br /> <br /> Doctor Primoris\u2019 Universe is the Primorium ( he was always the more egotistical of the Trio). I\u2019m thinking he may call his branch of Trinity the Nova Foundation, or Newman Foundation. Eventually he guts it, experiments on his world takes the Novas he wants and leaves the world to crumble while he Vanishes, though secretly he goes to Universe Null where none of them survived the Hammersmith Incident and thus no Trinity Continuum and thus he arrives with an army of Supermen, with default tech over a century ahead of the curve, and his elites sporting even greater tech. They conquer this world and keep tabs on the other three Universes and Work on breaching the Barrier beyond just the 3 (secretly 4) Universe and gaining access to infinite potential. With no one to stop him or reign in his accesses he forms a World Breaker Dynasty, Colonizes the Solar System and sets up Homo Sapien Novus as the next step for Humanity, or at least as the top of a caste system. The Newman Foundation is practically cannibalizes by the rest of Trinity and the remanents are untrusted and the two other Universe sort of commit predatory practices on this Universe owing the least loyalty to it and exploiting more then protecting or guiding it. Still the Newman Foundation has the most Novas, virtually the only Novas, of Trinity and that is enough to achieve miracles.<br /> <br /> Mercer was able to Cross Worlds rather then jump through time, seemingly he is limited to the three Universes, secretly he discovered Universe Null before Doctor Primoris, and May have been the first to dip into the greater Multiverse.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mercer at first shared information and was the go between for Bhurano and Donighal. They eventually discovered the Moon was somewhat more hollow then expected and had an Uncertain Casuality Field in its core. This promoted a naturally thin barrier between worlds that Trinity could exploit to create a Trinity of Gates deep under the Moons Surface as the primary means of travel between Universes. Later Primoris discovers the Zwave from the Hammersmith Incident left it\u2019s touch upon Mars and Mars had a weaker yet larger Uncertain Casuality Field Under it\u2019s surface. He uses hidden Subterranean Mars Bases to keep tabs on all the Universes.<br /> <br /> Hammersmith collected a Think tank that included Tesla and Mycroft Holmes and several other adventurers and men of science to gather info in the form of his miraculous Journals. The first Journal Hammersmith discovered was Da Vinci\u2019s Secret Journal, right after he had a correspondence with Einstein about his Quantum theories. Some of his other Journals included the Journal of the Black Tulku partially shared to him by Lamont Cranston, and the Journal of Mars kept by Ulysses Braxton. Hammersmith was convinced that Da Vinci discovered the secret to Immortality and managed to pierce the Universal Shell and found an Eternal City between his and two other Universes. Part of the Telluric Engine Experiment was intended to grant Hammersmith Immortality.<br /> <br /> The Doyen like in the normal Continuum kept an eye on Earth after the Hammersmith event and put up a Null field to prevent another one. Really only the Primorium broke the Null Field and re-alerted the Doyen. Eventually the Doyen will gather info on the Trinity pocket Multiverse and will likely ally with their counterparts. So by the time of the Nova Age for the normal Continuum this pocket Continuum will suffer asymmetrical warfare from the Worldbreaker Dynasty and the Doyen first on the Primorium.<br /> <br /> <br /> Later Primorium projects will lead to creating gateways to other worlds starting with the Pangea Universe a world still stuck in the Dinosaur era without humanity.<br /> <br /> Fun will be had by all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-22T06:54:59-08:00","id":1290744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1190042-the-trinity-multiverse?p=1190134#post1190134\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am planning some timeline travel between divergent histories<br /> <br /> Timeline Alpha: core timeline through Adventure!, Trinity Core, Aberrant, Anima, and Aeon<br /> <br /> Timeline Beta: core timeline until N-Day does not occur and Trinity Core action setting hones to the real world (includes comparatively harder scifi Expanse-style future with Talents, but no Novas or Promethean Chambers)<br /> <br /> Timeline Gamma: same as Alpha through Aberrant, but then the Aberrant War culminates in full burn - Mad Max/Fallout style setting ensues<br /> <br /> Timeline Delta: Inspiration Age (Adventure!) never ends and heroes and villains divert course of history leading to pulp space exploration by competing democratic, communist, and fascist powers by mid-20th Century, discovering a Burroughs-style Planetary Romance solar system<br /> <br /> Timeline Epsilon: Mal uses the Trinity test to set off the Nova Age in '45, Silver Age style setting by the 60s, Mal-Victorious Nova god kings ruling over human civilizations in their image in a 21st Century setting<br /> <br /> Timeline Zeta: War of the Worlds invasion in the 1890s, humanity rebuilding with the alien tech in the Edwardian Era create Promethean Chambers 200 years early<br /> <br /> Timeline Omega: Psions fail to rise against Colony's invasion; Aberrants destroy humanity</div> </div> </div> </div>Email me when the Kickstarter is being set up. I want your book.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"at